{"parentUuid":"6ea34fa8-cdcb-4a8a-92b8-57a5cb37963d","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1276a829-abfd-4b9a-912f-71b2aae9668e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ENb2zQJwY1W4Ue3gtJ5UC1","type":"tool_result","content":"1-free-file-opened-turn.jpg\n2-expert-to-standard-crossing.jpg\n3-cache-check-and-balance-panel.jpg\n4-welcome-back-v1-subscriber.jpg\n5-fresh-install-example.jpg\n6-fresh-install-example-sliced.jpg\n7-fresh-install-home.jpg\napp-stopped\nprobe-stopped\n      79\n 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)\n21:3. Fixed. On a truly fresh install, \"I don't have a printer here\" refused with \"No local printer profile is installed\", because no vendor is installed yet. It now installs the bundled \"Generic Klip\n26:- Open. A fresh-install example shows the chip's warning triangle and \"from the file\", though the file names no printer, because `printer_from_file` is true for any system profile that is not a nam\n27:- The example opens with \"1 print issue\": its three stacked objects trigger OrcaSlicer's collision warning in `Print.cpp`. It sliced anyway.\n40:- Returning users do not get the Home welcome. A person with an agent already configured skips it. `open_onboarding_example` kept.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"c1df54b8-f7fa-4551-bbee-2bce943b49d6","timestamp":"2026-11-02T15:48:27.969Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"1-free-file-opened-turn.jpg\n2-expert-to-standard-crossing.jpg\n3-cache-check-and-balance-panel.jpg\n4-welcome-back-v1-subscriber.jpg\n5-fresh-install-example.jpg\n6-fresh-install-example-sliced.jpg\n7-fresh-install-home.jpg\napp-stopped\nprobe-stopped\n      79\n 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)\n21:3. Fixed. On a truly fresh install, \"I don't have a printer here\" refused with \"No local printer profile is installed\", because no vendor is installed yet. It now installs the bundled \"Generic Klip\n26:- Open. A fresh-install example shows the chip's warning triangle and \"from the file\", though the file names no printer, because `printer_from_file` is true for any system profile that is not a nam\n27:- The example opens with \"1 print issue\": its three stacked objects trigger OrcaSlicer's collision warning in `Print.cpp`. It sliced anyway.\n40:- Returning users do not get the Home welcome. A person with an agent already configured skips it. `open_onboarding_example` kept.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6ea34fa8-cdcb-4a8a-92b8-57a5cb37963d","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/credits-onboarding","sessionId":"f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"temporal-enchanting-muffin"}
