{"parentUuid":"41521d59-24da-4a27-b03e-2cd32b60b826","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgeN6PgKmzLKy3jNsZ7Fa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EmpQ2xopUWqDg6JCDadJu6","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_756f4482-e5c7-45b4-bc36-5e6db3b079ef/credits-onboarding-flags.md","offset":20,"limit":9},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1952,"cache_read_input_tokens":179602,"output_tokens":464,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1952,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":464,"cache_read_input_tokens":179602,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1952,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1952},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01EmpQ2xopUWqDg6JCDadJu6":{"file_path":"/Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_756f4482-e5c7-45b4-bc36-5e6db3b079ef/credits-onboarding-flags.md","offset":20,"limit":9}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgeN6P5Minqm4dDefYnWj","requestRef":"6574f04d-a486-403c-aa65-0a4b0083c8dc","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"computer-use","attributionMcpTool":"app_release","type":"assistant","uuid":"9f78aed3-a273-4c6a-b569-d6ad443d8457","timestamp":"2026-11-02T15:48:30.410Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/credits-onboarding","sessionId":"f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"temporal-enchanting-muffin"}
{"parentUuid":"9f78aed3-a273-4c6a-b569-d6ad443d8457","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1276a829-abfd-4b9a-912f-71b2aae9668e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EmpQ2xopUWqDg6JCDadJu6","type":"tool_result","content":"20\t2. Fixed. Retrying failed presets when nothing more imports cleared the partial screen and jumped to Printer setup with \"could not be imported\", though one preset had imported. It now stays on the partial screen and says \"These profiles still could not be imported.\" Tested only by the real-app run, because no automated test reaches this code.\n21\t3. Fixed. On a truly fresh install, \"I don't have a printer here\" refused with \"No local printer profile is installed\", because no vendor is installed yet. It now installs the bundled \"Generic Klipper Printer\" 0.4, whose preset is \"MyKlipper 0.4 nozzle\". The example's 3MF does NOT carry printer or process settings: it holds only `3D/3dmodel.model`, `Metadata/model_settings.config` and `Metadata/slice_info.config`, so nothing in the file can say what to install. Harness mode `--fresh-example` guards it; it was run with the fix removed and fails with the old refusal. In the real app, the example opened with 3 objects and sliced: 3 filaments, 202 g, 7 h 8 min. The model uses filament slots 1 to 3 on a printer with one extruder, so a person who sends it to a real single-toolhead printer would get tool changes. The example step says no physical printer is required.\n22\t\n23\t## Found by the live local chats, 2026-11-02\n24\t\n25\t- Not fixed. The gateway logs \"could not keep a chat request\" for every Standard request through OpenRouter, with `JSONDecodeError: Expecting value: line 1 column 2`, the error `json.loads('[DONE]')` gives. `_collect` in `web_ent/jusprin/v2/gateway.py` (committed in 906752ee3e) parses every event as JSON. The chat still works; those requests are not kept. That OpenRouter sends `[DONE]` is inferred from the error text; the stream itself was not read.\n26\t- Open. A fresh-install example shows the chip's warning triangle and \"from the file\", though the file names no printer, because `printer_from_file` is true for any system profile that is not a named printer.\n27\t- The example opens with \"1 print issue\": its three stacked objects trigger OrcaSlicer's collision warning in `Print.cpp`. It sliced anyway.\n28\t"}]},"uuid":"c8af6bd2-1921-4598-8d33-a8bd258e9662","timestamp":"2026-11-02T15:48:30.451Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_756f4482-e5c7-45b4-bc36-5e6db3b079ef/credits-onboarding-flags.md","content":"2. Fixed. Retrying failed presets when nothing more imports cleared the partial screen and jumped to Printer setup with \"could not be imported\", though one preset had imported. It now stays on the partial screen and says \"These profiles still could not be imported.\" Tested only by the real-app run, because no automated test reaches this code.\n3. Fixed. On a truly fresh install, \"I don't have a printer here\" refused with \"No local printer profile is installed\", because no vendor is installed yet. It now installs the bundled \"Generic Klipper Printer\" 0.4, whose preset is \"MyKlipper 0.4 nozzle\". The example's 3MF does NOT carry printer or process settings: it holds only `3D/3dmodel.model`, `Metadata/model_settings.config` and `Metadata/slice_info.config`, so nothing in the file can say what to install. Harness mode `--fresh-example` guards it; it was run with the fix removed and fails with the old refusal. In the real app, the example opened with 3 objects and sliced: 3 filaments, 202 g, 7 h 8 min. The model uses filament slots 1 to 3 on a printer with one extruder, so a person who sends it to a real single-toolhead printer would get tool changes. The example step says no physical printer is required.\n\n## Found by the live local chats, 2026-11-02\n\n- Not fixed. The gateway logs \"could not keep a chat request\" for every Standard request through OpenRouter, with `JSONDecodeError: Expecting value: line 1 column 2`, the error `json.loads('[DONE]')` gives. `_collect` in `web_ent/jusprin/v2/gateway.py` (committed in 906752ee3e) parses every event as JSON. The chat still works; those requests are not kept. That OpenRouter sends `[DONE]` is inferred from the error text; the stream itself was not read.\n- Open. A fresh-install example shows the chip's warning triangle and \"from the file\", though the file names no printer, because `printer_from_file` is true for any system profile that is not a named printer.\n- The example opens with \"1 print issue\": its three stacked objects trigger OrcaSlicer's collision warning in `Print.cpp`. It sliced anyway.\n","numLines":9,"startLine":20,"totalLines":93}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9f78aed3-a273-4c6a-b569-d6ad443d8457","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/credits-onboarding","sessionId":"f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"temporal-enchanting-muffin"}
