{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"f57d8b7e-fd5a-4daf-9378-2e3d21342f7c","hash":"4979033d2ac5210dc86c48f87a03b8c3394cb2f5cc22c29cc4c1a03775539979","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01H7immAPif7qqbusfVVpNoQ","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_756f4482-e5c7-45b4-bc36-5e6db3b079ef/credits-onboarding-flags.md","old_string":"- Open. A fresh-install example shows the chip's warning triangle and \"from the file\", though the file names no printer, because `printer_from_file` is true for any system profile that is not a named printer.\n- The example opens with \"1 print issue\": its three stacked objects trigger OrcaSlicer's collision warning in `Print.cpp`. It sliced anyway.","new_string":"- Fixed, and this replaces item 3's example details above. The example no longer opens the OrcaSliced 3MF, which had three stacked objects, three filaments and a collision warning. It opens `resources/handy_models/3DBenchy.drc`. `resources/profiles` holds no printable model. The printer is now saved under its own name, \"Generic Klipper Printer\", the way normal printer setup does, so the chip shows no warning triangle or \"from the file\". There is no rule specific to onboarding. Real-app result on an empty data folder: one object, one filament, ~44 min, 12 g, $0.23, no print issue. Cost: Home shows a printer card \"Generic Klipper Printer, Not connected\".\n- Fixed. Choosing a printer on an empty project wrote change rows, and Home listed any empty project with rows, so a blank \"Untitled\" card appeared beside the opened file. `authored_head` in `Workspace/ProjectAutosave.cpp` no longer lists an empty project whose only history is printer, filament or process choices. A chat on an empty plate stays listed. The empty project's folder stays on disk, hidden. This applies to every path that picks a printer on an empty project, not only the example. Only the example path was run; that other paths left a blank card before is inferred from the code."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LNNY7zykjG39SShNehbkQY","name":"mcp__ccd_turn__wrap_up","input":{"recap":"The fresh-install example now opens 3DBenchy on a saved Generic Klipper Printer with no warnings and no blank project card, and there is no onboarding-only rule. All test suites and a real-app run pass. Nothing is committed, and the OpenRouter logging bug is still unfixed.","ask":"Should I fix the OpenRouter bug that stops Standard requests being kept?","actions":[{"label":"Yes, fix it","message":"Yes, fix the gateway bug that stops Standard requests through OpenRouter from being kept."},{"label":"Not now","message":"Leave the OpenRouter logging bug for now."}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
