{"parentUuid":"2f726531-c2f2-46df-82ba-557da59338ce","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgeN7LnE53jqCaU7Au7Mx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fresh-install example now works with no warnings and no special onboarding rule. Yes, \"Drop the warning\" would have been hard-coding it to disappear only during onboarding, so I didn't do that. Nothing is committed.\n\n**What the example does now**\n- **File:** it opens `resources/handy_models/3DBenchy.drc`, the Benchy boat bundled with the app. `resources/profiles` has no printable 3MF or STL, only printer images, so the file had to come from `handy_models`.\n- **Printer:** it installs Generic Klipper Printer and saves it under that name, the same way normal printer setup does.\n\n**Why the file alone wasn't enough**\n- The warning triangle and \"from the file\" on the printer chip depend only on the printer, so no file could remove them. Saving the printer under its own name did.\n- The old file caused the other problems: its three stacked objects produced the print issue, the extra filaments and the changed settings. Benchy has none of those.\n\n**Real app, on an empty data folder**\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Printer chip | \"Generic Klipper Printer · 0.4\", no warning |\n| Filament | One (Generic PLA) |\n| Print issues | None shown |\n| Slice | About 44 min, 12 g, $0.23 |\n| Projects on Home | One, 3DBenchy |\n\n**Two things you may want to look at**\n- **Printer card on Home:** Home now shows \"Generic Klipper Printer · Not connected\". That's the cost of having no special rule, because the printer really is installed.\n- **A change to autosave beyond the example:** choosing a printer on an empty project used to make Home list it as a blank \"Untitled\" card beside the opened file. Now an empty project isn't listed if its only history is printer, filament or process choices; a chat on an empty plate still is. From the code, this should also remove the blank card after normal printer setup, but I only ran the example path. The empty project's folder stays on disk, hidden.\n\n**Tests:** all of these pass:\n- Agent page tests (651) and Home page tests (130), plus their type checks\n- `jusprin_tests` (151), `agent_bridge_tests` (506) and `shell_theme_tests` (14)\n- `brand_tokens_tests`, with only its 2 expected failures\n- the default shell harness (600 checks)\n- `--fresh-example`, including new checks in both directions for the blank-card rule\n\nThe screenshots are attached and saved in [live-check-2026-11-02](live-check-2026-11-02):\n- [5-fresh-install-example.jpg](live-check-2026-11-02/5-fresh-install-example.jpg)\n- [6-fresh-install-example-sliced.jpg](live-check-2026-11-02/6-fresh-install-example-sliced.jpg)\n- [7-fresh-install-home.jpg](live-check-2026-11-02/7-fresh-install-home.jpg)\n\n**Still unfixed:** the gateway logs \"could not keep a chat request\" on every Standard request through OpenRouter. Chats still work, but those requests aren't kept. The cause looks like `_collect` in `web_ent/jusprin/v2/gateway.py` trying to parse OpenRouter's `[DONE]` line as JSON, which I inferred from the error text."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1236,"cache_read_input_tokens":182862,"output_tokens":1084,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1236,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1084,"cache_read_input_tokens":182862,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1236,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1236},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,